From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:30:19 -0300
Subject: video/hdmi: pad the top-and-bottom vendor InfoFrame to six bytes

HDMI 1.4b requires the 3D_Ext_Data byte only for side by side (half),
so a top-and-bottom vendor InfoFrame went out with a 5-byte body. Sinks
exist that engage 3D only on a 6-byte body: a Sony KDL-46HX855 ignores
the 5-byte top-and-bottom announcement and engages on the same stream
with a zero byte appended, and Adrian Betschart found the same behind
JVC projectors (amd-gfx, v3 2/3). The appended byte is not 3D_Ext_Data,
which HDMI 1.4a section 8.2.3 rules out for 3D_Structure 0000 to 0111:
it is a reserved zero byte, which Table 8-11 allows up to PB(Nv). The
unpacker already accepts it.

Assisted-by: Claude-Opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 084d325059f3c1cb5a22222ac7292a31e06fa288)
---
 drivers/video/hdmi.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/hdmi.c b/drivers/video/hdmi.c
index 45b42f14a7..443de11f56 100644
--- a/drivers/video/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/video/hdmi.c
@@ -551,8 +551,14 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(hdmi_vendor_infoframe_init);
 
 static int hdmi_vendor_infoframe_length(const struct hdmi_vendor_infoframe *frame)
 {
-	/* for side by side (half) we also need to provide 3D_Ext_Data */
-	if (frame->s3d_struct >= HDMI_3D_STRUCTURE_SIDE_BY_SIDE_HALF)
+	/*
+	 * Side by side (half) carries 3D_Ext_Data. Top and bottom has none
+	 * (HDMI 1.4a, 8.2.3), but gets a reserved zero byte after PB5, which
+	 * Table 8-11 allows (reserved bytes up to PB(Nv)): sinks that only
+	 * engage 3D on a 6-byte body exist (a Sony KDL-46HX855; JVC projectors).
+	 */
+	if (frame->s3d_struct >= HDMI_3D_STRUCTURE_SIDE_BY_SIDE_HALF ||
+	    frame->s3d_struct == HDMI_3D_STRUCTURE_TOP_AND_BOTTOM)
 		return 6;
 	else if (frame->vic != 0 || frame->s3d_struct != HDMI_3D_STRUCTURE_INVALID)
 		return 5;
